{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>About midnight.</b> Some grammarians say כחצות is a verb, and the meaning is 'when half the night is equally divided,' for they wanted to compare it to ויהי בחצי הלילה (Exodus 12:29). It is known that a sage has no ability to know the precise moment of midday except with great effort using large instruments of bronze, all the more so midnight, which is harder. In my opinion there is no need for any of this, for the meaning of כחצת הלילה is 'when the first half of the night has passed and so on,' in the remaining half — as in בחצי הלילה (Exodus 12:29). The trustworthy witness: ויהי בחצי הלילה ויחרד האיש וילפת (Ruth 3:8); 'At midnight I rise to give thanks to You' (Psalms 119:62)." "The meaning of 'I go out' [refers to] the decree going out from HaShem."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Resolved 'הפועל' as referring to כחצות being analyzed as a verb form, per the grammarians Ibn Ezra cites."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:22.687852849Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}